++{"class_id": 3114, "class": "go-wasm-tailcall-stack-map-verifier", "title": "go-wasm-tailcall-stack-map-verifier", "description": "go-wasm-tailcall-stack-map-verifier", "answer_id": 4849, "language": "go", "environment": "go1.26", "version": "1.26", "solution": "# Verified Solution: `go-wasm-tailcall-stack-map-verifier`\n\nA deterministic, linear-time type verifier for a compact Wasm-like bytecode with indirect calls, tail calls, exception edges, multi-value returns, and bounded linear memory.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Root-cause analysis\n\nThe problem class is not one bug — it is a family of soundness and complexity traps that appear when you validate a typed stack machine with structured control flow:\n\n| Trap | Why it breaks |\n|---|---|\n| **Naive CFG path enumeration** | Enumerating every path through nested `block`/`if`/`loop` is exponential in nesting depth. An adversarial program with `N` nested blocks has `2^N` paths, so the verifier hangs. |\n| **Coarse join (\"any type\")** | If a join point accepts `Bot`/`any`, a value of one type can flow into a slot that expects another, so ill-typed programs are accepted. Joins must be *exact*. |\n| **Ad-hoc safepoints** | Stack maps at calls must contain the precise live type of every operand slot. Reading them from a partially-popped stack yields wrong GC metadata. |\n| **Missing tail-call frame check** | `return_call` replaces the current frame. If callee results ≠ caller results (or params don't match the operand stack), the machine returns the wrong arity/types. |\n| **Exceptions treated as plain blocks** | A `catch` handler begins with the tag payload on the stack. Forgetting to type the payload lets a `throw i64` reach a handler expecting `i32`. |\n| **Recursive descent** | A verifier that recurses on block nesting overflows the Go stack on deep programs. |\n\n**Key insight.** Wasm control flow is *structured*. You do not need path enumeration: a single forward pass driven by an explicit **control-frame stack** validates every join at block boundaries (`end`, `else`, `catch`). Each instruction is visited once → **O(n)** time and **O(depth)** space, regardless of path count. Unreachable code is handled with **stack polymorphism** (`Bot`), and dead safepoints are pruned by a reachability bit.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The algorithm\n\nPer function, keep:\n\n- `opds []ValType` — the abstract operand stack.\n- `ctrls []ctrlFrame` — one frame per open `block`/`loop`/`if`/`try` (plus one implicit frame for the function body). A frame records `{opcode, startTypes, endTypes, height, unreachable}`.\n\nCore operations (standard Wasm validation algorithm, adapted):\n\n- `popVal`: if the current frame is `unreachable` and the stack is at `height`, return `Bot` (polymorphic). Otherwise pop; popping at/below `height` is underflow.\n- `pushCtrl(op,in,out)`: record `height=len(opds)`, push `in`.\n- `popCtrl`: `popVals(endTypes)`, require `len(opds)==height`, unwind.\n- `unreachable`: truncate `opds` to `height`, set the frame flag.\n- `labelTypes(frame)`: `startTypes` for `loop` (branch target = header), `endTypes` otherwise.\n- `br l`: pop `labelTypes(ctrls[l])`, then `unreachable`.\n- `end`: `popCtrl`, push `endTypes`; an `if` with no `else` requires `params == results`.\n- `else`: `popCtrl` (must be `if`), push a new frame with the same types.\n- `catch tag`: `popCtrl` (must be `try`/`catch`), push a `catch` frame whose inputs are the **tag payload** `tag.Params`, `endTypes` unchanged. A `try` without `catch` is rejected.\n- `throw tag`: pop the tag payload, then `unreachable` (handler bodies are validated independently with the payload on top).\n- `return_call f`: pop callee params; require `callee.Results == currentFunc.Results`; `unreachable`.\n- `load`/`store`: require a declared memory, `offset + size <= maxPages*65536`, and `align <= naturalAlign`.\n\n**Joins are exact** because both the fall-through path (`end`) and every branch path (`br`) must produce precisely `endTypes`. There is no path enumeration, so deep nesting stays linear.\n\n**Safepoints.** At each reachable `call`, `call_indirect`, `return_call`, `return_call_indirect`, `throw`, and `return`, record a `StackMap{Func, PC, Op, Stack, Locals}` taken *before* popping arguments. `Bot` cannot occur in a reachable map.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Exact fix — complete source\n\n### `go.mod`\n\n```go\nmodule wasmverify\n\ngo 1.26\n```\n\n### `verify.go`\n\n```go\n// Package wasmverify implements a deterministic, linear-time type checker for a\n// compact WebAssembly-like bytecode. It supports indirect calls, tail calls,\n// exception edges, multi-value returns and bounded linear memory.\n//\n// The verifier is a single forward pass over each function body driven by an\n// explicit control-frame stack (no recursion).  Because the control flow is\n// structured, joins are enforced by the block/catch/loop frames and every\n// instruction is visited exactly once.  This makes verification O(n) and immune\n// to exponential path enumeration on adversarially nested programs.\npackage wasmverify\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n)\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Types\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n// ValType is an abstract value type.\ntype ValType uint8\n\nconst (\n\tI32 ValType = iota\n\tI64\n\tF32\n\tF64\n\tFuncRef\n\t// Bot is the bottom type that inhabits polymorphic stack slots in dead\n\t// (unreachable) code.  It is compatible with every type.\n\tBot\n)\n\nfunc (t ValType) String() string {\n\tswitch t {\n\tcase I32:\n\t\treturn \"i32\"\n\tcase I64:\n\t\treturn \"i64\"\n\tcase F32:\n\t\treturn \"f32\"\n\tcase F64:\n\t\treturn \"f64\"\n\tcase FuncRef:\n\t\treturn \"funcref\"\n\tcase Bot:\n\t\treturn \"bot\"\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"type(%d)\", t)\n\t}\n}\n\n// FuncType is a function signature.\ntype FuncType struct {\n\tParams  []ValType\n\tResults []ValType\n}\n\nfunc (ft FuncType) String() string {\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"(%s)->(%s)\", joinTypes(ft.Params), joinTypes(ft.Results))\n}\n\nfunc joinTypes(ts []ValType) string {\n\ts := \"\"\n\tfor i, t := range ts {\n\t\tif i > 0 {\n\t\t\ts += \" \"\n\t\t}\n\t\ts += t.String()\n\t}\n\treturn s\n}\n\nfunc equalTypes(a, b []ValType) bool {\n\tif len(a) != len(b) {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tfor i := range a {\n\t\tif a[i] != b[i] {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn true\n}\n\nfunc cloneTypes(ts []ValType) []ValType {\n\tif ts == nil {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\treturn append([]ValType(nil), ts...)\n}\n\n// BlockType describes the parameters and results of a structured block.\ntype BlockType struct {\n\tParams  []ValType\n\tResults []ValType\n}\n\n// MemArg describes a memory access immediate.\ntype MemArg struct {\n\tAlign  uint32 // log2 of the alignment in bytes\n\tOffset uint32 // static byte offset\n}\n\n// Memory is a bounded linear memory, measured in 64 KiB pages.\ntype Memory struct {\n\tMinPages uint32\n\tMaxPages uint32\n}\n\nfunc (m *Memory) byteLen() uint64 {\n\treturn uint64(m.MaxPages) * 65536\n}\n\n// TagType describes an exception tag (its payload is the parameter list).\ntype TagType struct {\n\tParams []ValType\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Instructions\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n// Op is an opcode.\ntype Op uint8\n\nconst (\n\tOpI32Const Op = iota\n\tOpI64Const\n\tOpF32Const\n\tOpF64Const\n\tOpLocalGet\n\tOpLocalSet\n\tOpLocalTee\n\tOpGlobalGet\n\tOpGlobalSet\n\tOpDrop\n\tOpSelect\n\tOpI32Add\n\tOpI32Sub\n\tOpI32Mul\n\tOpI64Add\n\tOpI32Eqz\n\tOpI32Eq\n\tOpI32LtS\n\tOpCall\n\tOpCallIndirect\n\tOpReturnCall\n\tOpReturnCallIndirect\n\tOpReturn\n\tOpBlock\n\tOpLoop\n\tOpIf\n\tOpElse\n\tOpEnd\n\tOpBr\n\tOpBrIf\n\tOpBrTable\n\tOpThrow\n\tOpTry\n\tOpCatch\n\tOpLoad\n\tOpStore\n)\n\nfunc (o Op) String() string {\n\tnames := []string{\n\t\t\"i32.const\", \"i64.const\", \"f32.const\", \"f64.const\",\n\t\t\"local.get\", \"local.set\", \"local.tee\", \"global.get\", \"global.set\",\n\t\t\"drop\", \"select\", \"i32.add\", \"i32.sub\", \"i32.mul\", \"i64.add\",\n\t\t\"i32.eqz\", \"i32.eq\", \"i32.lt_s\",\n\t\t\"call\", \"call_indirect\", \"return_call\", \"return_call_indirect\",\n\t\t\"return\", \"block\", \"loop\", \"if\", \"else\", \"end\",\n\t\t\"br\", \"br_if\", \"br_table\", \"throw\", \"try\", \"catch\", \"load\", \"store\",\n\t}\n\tif int(o) < len(names) {\n\t\treturn names[o]\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"op(%d)\", o)\n}\n\n// Instr is a decoded instruction.\ntype Instr struct {\n\tOp    Op\n\tImm   int64 // constant value / local, global, func, type or tag index / branch depth\n\tType  ValType\n\tBlock BlockType\n\tMem   MemArg\n\t// OpBrTable only.\n\tTargets []int\n\tDefault int\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Module\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n// Func is a function definition. Locals excludes the parameters declared in\n// the signature (params come first, followed by Locals).\ntype Func struct {\n\tType   int\n\tLocals []ValType\n\tBody   []Instr\n}\n\n// Global is a module-level variable.\ntype Global struct {\n\tType    ValType\n\tMutable bool\n}\n\n// Module is a verifiable unit.\ntyp